{
  "adjustments": [
    {
      "target": "u1",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "The whole update remains supported. `P2:23`-`P2:24` and `P3:16`-`P3:17` show that heating while holding the target at the microwave succeeds directly, while `P1:29`-`P1:31`, `P4:6`-`P4:8`, and `P4:50` show opening, moving the target into the microwave, closing it, and then toggling it without heating ends unheated at the step limit. `M3` also reports that hold-and-invoke heat guidance was associated with success when the target was acquired, though that historical edit was joint. The wording does not conflict with multi-instance search because the condition is specifically being at a microwave while holding the target for a hot-object task.",
      "to": null
    },
    {
      "target": "u2",
      "focus": [
        "S",
        "C"
      ],
      "change": "Preserve the priority for a known location that still contains needed visible target instances, but make the collection guidance respect the observed one-object carry capacity: take one needed instance, deposit it, then return to that same known location for the next needed instance before searching unknown locations, unless the location is observed to no longer contain one. Keep the prohibition on taking more than the remaining required count.",
      "reason": "The direction is supported: `P5:11` shows three cds at dresser 1, but `P5:12` takes only one and the later search at `P5:16`-`P5:50` does not collect another from that known location. `P8:1`-`P8:11` and `P9:7`-`P9:10` show that returning to a known location or checking a new container can complete the task. However, the admissible set changes from `C75` to `C76` after taking cd 1: `C76` no longer offers take actions for the other cds, indicating one-object carry capacity. The original instruction to collect multiple needed instances “in that visit” is therefore not executable. The revision keeps known-location priority and the remaining-count cap while specifying the feasible follow-through. It also coordinates with u4: a known target-containing location overrides the anti-revisit rule. The return-until-exhausted behavior remains unverified under limited history and is exposed in check c2.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n-- When a task requires multiple target instances and a known location contains one or more still-needed visible instances of the target, prioritize going there and taking the needed number up to the remaining required count before searching other unknown locations.\n-- If a location exposes more than one needed instance, collect as many as are needed in that visit rather than taking only one and leaving the others behind.\n+- When a task requires multiple target instances and a known location contains one or more still-needed visible instances of the target, prioritize going there and taking a needed instance, never more than the remaining required count, before searching other unknown locations.\n+- You can normally carry only one object at a time. If that location still contains additional needed instances after you take one, remember the location and return to collect the next needed instance after depositing the held instance; do not search other unknown locations before exhausting the needed instances from that known location unless it is observed to no longer contain one.\n - Do not take extra instances beyond the remaining required count.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "u3",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "The whole update is supported and its exception prevents overconstraint. `P5:15` places cd 1 in drawer 1, then `P5:31` moves it to drawer 2 while the task is still unmet; P6 places candles in different drawers and shuttles them at `P6:26`, `P6:36`, `P6:42`, and `P6:47`; both fail at the step limit. In contrast, `P8:4` and `P8:11` consolidate both newspapers on sofa 1, and `P9:4` and `P9:10` consolidate both saltshakers on sidetable 1, both succeeding. The clause for unspecified target receptacles covers tasks such as “in drawer” while still allowing a suitable receptacle to be chosen once. It does not conflict with u2, which returns to the target source, because u3 governs the destination receptacle.",
      "to": null
    },
    {
      "target": "u4",
      "focus": [
        "S",
        "C"
      ],
      "change": "Keep the preference for unsearched candidate locations over rechecking known-empty ones, the known-target-location exception, and the anti-toggling/anti-shuttling guidance. Broaden the candidate object to open surfaces as well as containers, explicitly including countertops, diningtables, coffeetables, dressers, tvstands, and other open surfaces. Add that the Actor should use the current admissible go-to commands to identify remaining candidates and, unless a known target-containing location has priority, prefer a candidate not just checked in recent history rather than cycling through the same subset.",
      "reason": "The search direction is supported by `P5:16`-`P5:50` and `P7:43`-`P7:48`, where previously checked empty shelves or drawers are revisited and the runs end at the step limit. `P8:8`-`P8:11` supports returning to a known target-containing location, and `P9:7`-`P9:10` supports trying a new container. However, `M2` reports a prior broad-search/anti-revisit edit whose candidate repeatedly cycled among inspected locations and never visited diningtable 1, a plausible open surface; `M1` likewise reports extended rechecking of known-empty shelves. The original examples omit open surfaces such as diningtables, countertops, coffeetables, dressers, and tvstands. The revision expands scope to those surfaces and gives a feasible selection rule using admissible go-to commands and recent history. The recent-history preference is an experimental implementation under the Actor’s limited history; check c4 assesses coverage and step cost.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n-- While a multi-instance task is unmet and unsearched candidate receptacles remain, check those unsearched receptacles before revisiting receptacles already observed to be empty or already checked without finding the target.\n-- If a previously visited location was seen to contain a needed target instance but you did not collect it, treat that location as a priority; otherwise do not repeatedly toggle or open/close the same container or shuttle the same object between locations.\n-- Expand search to all types of candidate containers, including remaining drawers, shelves, cabinets, and sidetables, rather than cycling through the same subset.\n+- While a multi-instance task is unmet and unsearched candidate receptacles or open surfaces remain, check those unsearched candidates before revisiting a location already observed to be empty or already checked without finding the target. Use the current admissible go-to commands to identify remaining candidate locations, and, unless a known target-containing location has priority, prefer a candidate not just checked in the recent history rather than cycling through the same subset.\n+- If a previously visited location was seen to contain a needed target instance but you did not collect it, treat that location as a priority; otherwise do not repeatedly toggle or open/close the same container or shuttle the same object between locations.\n+- Expand search to all types of candidate containers and surfaces named in the scene, including remaining drawers, shelves, cabinets, sidetables, countertops, diningtables, coffeetables, dressers, tvstands, and other open surfaces, rather than cycling through the same subset.\n"
      }
    }
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "update_ids": [
        "u1"
      ],
      "question": "When the Actor is holding a target object at a microwave and a direct heat action is available, does it choose that direct heat action instead of opening or moving the object into the microwave first?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "update_ids": [
        "u2"
      ],
      "question": "For multi-instance tasks, after taking one needed instance from a known location, does the Actor deposit it and then return to that location to collect the remaining needed instances before searching other unknown locations, without taking more than the remaining required count?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "update_ids": [
        "u3"
      ],
      "question": "For multi-instance tasks, does the Actor place subsequent target instances in the receptacle already used for the first instance and avoid shuttling already-placed instances between receptacles?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c4",
      "update_ids": [
        "u4"
      ],
      "question": "When the target remains unmet, does the Actor select unsearched candidate containers or surfaces, including those beyond the current subset, before rechecking known-empty locations, while still returning to a known target-containing location when one is available?"
    }
  ]
}
